# Force LF line endings for all text files regardless of a checkout's local
# core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a Windows checkout (git's
# core.autocrlf=true default there) silently converts these to CRLF, which
# breaks things in ways that don't announce themselves: a CRLF shebang line
# makes direct execution (`./script.sh`) fail with a confusing "No such file
# or directory" naming the interpreter-plus-\r, a CRLF-terminated
# `set -euo pipefail` line fails with "pipefail: invalid option name", and a
# CRLF-terminated infra/egress_allowlist.txt breaks scripts/check_no_egress.sh's
# regex matching against every allowlist rule at once with no visible error
# -- all found the hard way, verifying changes locally on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf
